<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Further analysis</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Block-coordinate ascent in MI bounds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the formal proof for the proposition stated in <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Block-coordinate ascent via DV bound ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, establishing the theoretical foundation for monotonic MI increase under alternating optimization in the SDMI paradigm.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\cdot;\xi^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\cdot;\xi^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math> is concave, a gradient ascent step on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta^{(k+1)};\xi^{(k)})\geq J(\theta^{(k)};\xi^{(k)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta^{(k+1)};\xi^{(k)})\geq J(\theta^{(k)};\xi^{(k)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By smoothness of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and the bound <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}M\|\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}M\|\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|M(\theta^{(k+1)};\xi^{(k)})-M(\theta^{(k)};\xi^{(k)})\right|=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|M(\theta^{(k+1)};\xi^{(k)})-M(\theta^{(k)};\xi^{(k)})\right|=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">which yields</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta^{(k+1)},\xi^{(k)})\geq\mathcal{L}(\theta^{(k)},\xi^{(k)})-\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta^{(k+1)},\xi^{(k)})\geq\mathcal{L}(\theta^{(k)},\xi^{(k)})-\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">An identical argument applies to the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>-update. Chaining the two completes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Analyzing other variational bounds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Extending the analysis from <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Block-coordinate ascent via DV bound ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we examine other commonly used variational MI bounds in SSRL, including InfoNCE and JSD bounds mentioned in <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Mutual information and its variational bounds in SSRL ‣ 2 Related Work and Preliminaries ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, demonstrating that our framework generalizes beyond the DV bound.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>InfoNCE</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the InfoNCE loss between two representations <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> takes the form:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>InfoNCE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\left[\log\left(\frac{e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}}{\sum_{z_{B}^{\prime}}e^{T(z_{A},z_{B}^{\prime})}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\left[\log\left(\frac{e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}}{\sum_{z_{B}^{\prime}}e^{T(z_{A},z_{B}^{\prime})}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\left[T(z_{A},z_{B})-\log\left(\sum_{z_{B}^{\prime}}e^{T(z_{A},z_{B}^{\prime})}\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\left[T(z_{A},z_{B})-\log\left(\sum_{z_{B}^{\prime}}e^{T(z_{A},z_{B}^{\prime})}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is a similarity function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This loss can be interpreted as a lower bound on MI between <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Poole et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, such that:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\left[T(z_{A},z_{B})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})}\left[\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]\right]+\log N," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>InfoNCE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\left[T(z_{A},z_{B})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})}\left[\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]\right]+\log N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of negative samples.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Both the DV and the InfoNCE bounds follow the general structure: a joint term minus a marginal term. The only structural difference is that the DV bound aggregates globally before applying the logarithm:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]\quad\text{(global aggregation)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(global aggregation)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]\quad\text{(global aggregation)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">whereas InfoNCE applies the logarithm per sample:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})}\left[\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]\right]\quad\text{(local aggregation)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(local aggregation)</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})}\left[\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]\right]\quad\text{(local aggregation)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Although this difference affects the aggregation structure, both objectives satisfy the conditions of the proposition in <a href="#S3.E2" title="In Proposition ‣ 3.1 Block-coordinate ascent via DV bound ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and support monotonic improvement under alternating optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>JSD</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the JSD bound can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{JSD}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\!\big[-\log\!\big(1+e^{-T(z_{A},z_{B})}\big)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\!\big[\log\!\big(1+e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\big)\big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>JSD</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{JSD}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}\!\big[-\log\!\big(1+e^{-T(z_{A},z_{B})}\big)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\!\big[\log\!\big(1+e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\big)\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This form corresponds to a binary classification objective, distinguishing samples from the joint distribution versus the product of marginals. As with DV and InfoNCE, it has a ”joint term minus marginal term” structure, but instead of a log-sum-exp aggregation, it applies the softplus nonlinearity independently to each sample.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All three objectives (DV, InfoNCE, JSD) satisfy the conditions of the proposition in <a href="#S3.E2" title="In Proposition ‣ 3.1 Block-coordinate ascent via DV bound ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and allow monotonic improvement under alternating optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Moment‐based surrogates for the DV marginal term</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the complete mathematical derivation referenced in <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 From DV to Barlow Twins: A surrogate derivation ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> showing that the regularizers in Barlow Twins correspond to a second‐order Taylor expansion (cumulant expansion) of the DV bound’s marginal term.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">DV bound</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ground our approximation, we recall the DV bound (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.2 Mutual information and its variational bounds in SSRL ‣ 2 Related Work and Preliminaries ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Z_{A};Z_{B})\geq I_{\mathrm{DV}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})=\sup_{T\in\mathcal{F}}\left\{\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Joint term}}-\underbrace{\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]}_{\text{Marginal term}}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>DV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Joint term</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Marginal term</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Z_{A};Z_{B})\geq I_{\mathrm{DV}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})=\sup_{T\in\mathcal{F}}\left\{\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Joint term}}-\underbrace{\log\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\left[e^{T(z_{A},z_{B})}\right]}_{\text{Marginal term}}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is a critic function, chosen from a sufficiently expressive function class <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">CGF and Taylor expansion</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> be any bounded critic with</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(x,y)\in[a,b]\quad\text{for all }x,y," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(x,y)\in[a,b]\quad\text{for all }x,y,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">and define its CGF as</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(s)=\log\mathbb{E}[e^{sT}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(s)=\log\mathbb{E}[e^{sT}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded, <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is infinitely differentiable on <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, its <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th derivative at zero yields the <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th cumulant:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{n}=K^{(n)}(0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{n}=K^{(n)}(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In particular,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}(0)=\mathbb{E}[T],\quad K^{\prime\prime}(0)=\mathrm{Var}(T)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}(0)=\mathbb{E}[T],\quad K^{\prime\prime}(0)=\mathrm{Var}(T).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By Taylor’s theorem about <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(s)=s\,K^{\prime}(0)+\tfrac{1}{2}s^{2}\,K^{\prime\prime}(0)+R_{2}(s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(s)=s\,K^{\prime}(0)+\tfrac{1}{2}s^{2}\,K^{\prime\prime}(0)+R_{2}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}(s)=\tfrac{1}{6}s^{3}K^{(3)}(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}(s)=\tfrac{1}{6}s^{3}K^{(3)}(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in(0,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in(0,s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>, all derivatives of <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(s)</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded on <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, evaluating <a href="#A1.E22" title="In CGF and Taylor expansion ‣ A.3 Moment‐based surrogates for the DV marginal term ‣ Appendix A Further analysis ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> at <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|R_{2}(1)\bigr|\leq\frac{1}{6}\max_{s\in[0,1]}\bigl|K^{(3)}(s)\bigr|=\mathcal{O}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|R_{2}(1)\bigr|\leq\frac{1}{6}\max_{s\in[0,1]}\bigl|K^{(3)}(s)\bigr|=\mathcal{O}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">This constant can therefore be absorbed into a hyperparameter. Hence, the second-order approximation holds in full generality:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathbb{E}[e^{T}]=K(1)\approx\mathbb{E}[T]+\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{Var}(T)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{E}[e^{T}]=K(1)\approx\mathbb{E}[T]+\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{Var}(T).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Surrogate loss via mean-variance</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting <a href="#A1.E23" title="In CGF and Taylor expansion ‣ A.3 Moment‐based surrogates for the DV marginal term ‣ Appendix A Further analysis ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> into the DV bound (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.2 Mutual information and its variational bounds in SSRL ‣ 2 Related Work and Preliminaries ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) gives the surrogate MI lower bound</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{DV}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>DV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{DV}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\geq\;I_{\mathrm{Taylor\text{-}DV}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>Taylor</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>DV</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\geq\;I_{\mathrm{Taylor\text{-}DV}}(Z_{A};Z_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]-\left\{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\bigl[T(z_{A},z_{B})\bigr]\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]-\left\{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}\bigl[T(z_{A},z_{B})\bigr]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus one may construct a tractable loss as shown in <a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.4 From DV to Barlow Twins: A surrogate derivation ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Taylor\text{-}DV}}=-\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Joint term}}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Marginal mean term}}+\underbrace{\mathrm{Var}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Marginal variance term}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>Taylor</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>DV</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Joint term</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Marginal mean term</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Marginal variance term</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Taylor\text{-}DV}}=-\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A},z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Joint term}}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Marginal mean term}}+\underbrace{\mathrm{Var}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]}_{\text{Marginal variance term}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSSx4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Barlow Twins as a mean–variance surrogate</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start with <a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.4 From DV to Barlow Twins: A surrogate derivation ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}={z^{A}_{i}\,z^{B}_{i}},\quad T_{\cos}(z^{A},z^{B})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}={z^{A}\cdot z^{B}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>cos</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}={z^{A}_{i}\,z^{B}_{i}},\quad T_{\cos}(z^{A},z^{B})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}={z^{A}\cdot z^{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By the variance‐of‐a‐sum identity,</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\bigl[T(z^{A},z^{B})\bigr]=\mathrm{Var}\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}\Bigr)=\sum_{i,j=1}^{d}\mathrm{Cov}(X_{i},\,X_{j})=\sum_{i,j=1}^{d}\mathrm{Cov}(z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i},\;z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\bigl[T(z^{A},z^{B})\bigr]=\mathrm{Var}\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}\Bigr)=\sum_{i,j=1}^{d}\mathrm{Cov}(X_{i},\,X_{j})=\sum_{i,j=1}^{d}\mathrm{Cov}(z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i},\;z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Barlow Twins reduces the surrogate in <a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.4 From DV to Barlow Twins: A surrogate derivation ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> to an alignment term and a tractable approximation of the marginal variance by applying batch normalization, ensuring</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})}[z^{A}_{i}]=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{B})}[z^{B}_{i}]\approx 0\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]\approx 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})}[z^{A}_{i}]=\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{B})}[z^{B}_{i}]\approx 0\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathbb{E}_{p(z_{A})p(z_{B})}[T(z_{A},z_{B})]\approx 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{A}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{A}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{B}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{B}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th coordinate of views <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The regularization terms in Barlow Twins are constructed using batch-level statistics, specifically, the <em id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cross-correlation matrix</em> between features across the two views:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ij}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}z^{A}_{n,i}\cdot z^{B}_{n,j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ij}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}z^{A}_{n,i}\cdot z^{B}_{n,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{A}_{n,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{A}_{n,i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{B}_{n,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{B}_{n,j}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th and <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th features of the <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample from each view in a batch of size <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. The diagonal elements <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ii}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ii}</annotation></semantics></math> appear in the alignment term of the loss, encouraging each feature to match across views, while the off-diagonal elements <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math> are penalized to reduce redundancy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To connect this to the variance term in <a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.4 From DV to Barlow Twins: A surrogate derivation ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, we analyze the variance of <a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.4 From DV to Barlow Twins: A surrogate derivation ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> under independent sampling:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{p(x)p(y)}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{d}z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}\right]=\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Cov}(z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i},\;z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{p(x)p(y)}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{d}z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}\right]=\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Cov}(z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i},\;z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">This covariance approximates a fourth-order moment:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(X_{i},X_{j})=\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}\,z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j}]-\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}]\,\cdot\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.225em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(X_{i},X_{j})=\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}\,z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j}]-\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}]\,\cdot\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming that the representations are approximately jointly Gaussian and decorrelated within each view (i.e., <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{A}_{j}]\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{A}_{j}]\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z^{B}_{i}z^{B}_{j}]\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z^{B}_{i}z^{B}_{j}]\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>), we can apply Isserlis’ theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Munthe-Kaas et al., 2025</a>)</cite> to approximate the fourth-order covariance terms:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i},\;z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j})\approx\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{j}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{i}]=C_{ij}C_{ji}\approx C_{ij}^{2},\quad\text{for }i\neq j." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i},\;z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{j})\approx\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{j}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[z^{A}_{j}z^{B}_{i}]=C_{ij}C_{ji}\approx C_{ij}^{2},\quad\text{for }i\neq j.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The variance thus approximates the sum of off-diagonal squared correlations:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left[\sum_{i}z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}\right]\approx\sum_{i\neq j}C_{ij}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left[\sum_{i}z^{A}_{i}z^{B}_{i}\right]\approx\sum_{i\neq j}C_{ij}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Putting everything together, the Taylor–DV surrogate yields <a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.4 From DV to Barlow Twins: A surrogate derivation ‣ 3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Taylor\text{-}DV}}\approx-\sum_{i=1}^{d}C_{ii}+\sum_{i\neq j}C_{ij}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Taylor</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>DV</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">≈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Taylor\text{-}DV}}\approx-\sum_{i=1}^{d}C_{ii}+\sum_{i\neq j}C_{ij}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSSx4.p14.1" class="ltx_p">which matches the structure of the empirical Barlow Twins loss: an alignment term encouraging the diagonal of the cross-correlation matrix to approach 1, and a decorrelation term penalizing off-diagonal elements.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Input informativeness</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the SDMI and JMI frameworks increase <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(z_{E};z_{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(z_{E};z_{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, their effectiveness depends on how this relates to the input <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. We formalize this intuition with the following conjecture.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conjecture.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the assumption of deterministic encoders, the MI between two distinct augmented views <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> is upper bounded by:</p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})\leq\min(I(x;z^{(1)});I(x;z^{(2)}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})\leq\min(I(x;z^{(1)});I(x;z^{(2)}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that MI between two random variables <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(A;B)=H(A)-H(A\mid B)=H(B)-H(B\mid A)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(A;B)=H(A)-H(A\mid B)=H(B)-H(B\mid A).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(1)}=f(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(1)}=f(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(2)}=f(x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(2)}=f(x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(2)}=g(x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(2)}=g(x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for SDMI) are deterministic functions of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(z^{(1)}\mid x)=0,\quad H(z^{(2)}\mid x)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(z^{(1)}\mid x)=0,\quad H(z^{(2)}\mid x)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(x;z^{(1)})=H(z^{(1)}),\quad I(x;z^{(2)})=H(z^{(2)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(x;z^{(1)})=H(z^{(1)}),\quad I(x;z^{(2)})=H(z^{(2)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">By definition,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})=H(z^{(1)})-H(z^{(1)}\mid z^{(2)})\leq H(z^{(1)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})=H(z^{(1)})-H(z^{(1)}\mid z^{(2)})\leq H(z^{(1)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the inequality follows from the non-negativity of conditional entropy, <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(z^{(1)}\mid z^{(2)})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(z^{(1)}\mid z^{(2)})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})\leq I(x;z^{(1)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})\leq I(x;z^{(1)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">By symmetry, we also have <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})\leq I(x;z^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(z^{(1)};z^{(2)})\leq I(x;z^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(z_{E};z^{(2)})\leq\min\bigl\{I(x;z^{(1)}),\,I(x;z^{(2)})\bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(z_{E};z^{(2)})\leq\min\bigl\{I(x;z^{(1)}),\,I(x;z^{(2)})\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Algorithms</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Detailed algorithmic descriptions for the canonical SDMI and JMI prototypes introduced in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Canonical SDMI and JMI prototypes ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and illustrated in <a href="#S4.F1" title="In 4 Experiments ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> are provided below. Following common SSRL practice  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2020a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grill et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen &amp; He, 2021</a>)</cite>, we adopt a symmetric loss by computing the objective over both view orderings.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>SDMI canonical form training procedure</h3>

<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>EM‑style Training Procedure of the SDMI Prototype</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Unlabeled dataset <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, encoders <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, temperature <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, number of epochs <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Trained encoder parameters <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.4.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E-Step: Update <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, freeze <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> </span>
