<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Optimal hyperparameters selected from sweep-2 for each model and dataset. LR = learning rate, WD = weight decay, Temp. = temperature. All models use a ResNet-18 encoder. For VICReg, we fix the similarity, variance, and covariance loss coefficients to 25.0, 25.0, and 1.0, respectively, and set a small numerical stability term <math id="A4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. These values remain constant across all runs.</figcaption>
