<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>ImageNet100 and TinyImageNet Training Configuration</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For both the ImageNet100 and TinyImageNet datasets, we adopt a uniform configuration across all models, with only a few dataset-specific adjustments.
The settings are summarized in <a href="#A4.T6" title="In D.3 ImageNet100 and TinyImageNet Training Configuration ‣ Appendix D Implementation details ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Hyperparameter settings used for all models trained on ImageNet100 and TinyImageNet.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ImageNet100</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TinyImageNet</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Encoder Backbone</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">ResNet-50</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">ResNet-18</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Epochs</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">800</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">1000</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Warmup Epochs</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">10</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">5</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Batch Size</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">512</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Initial Learning Rate</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.05</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">0.05</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning Rate Schedule</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Cosine decay</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">Cosine decay</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Weight Decay</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0001</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">0.0005</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Projection Layers</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">3</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Projection Dimension</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">256</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Feature Dimension</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">512</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">512</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note:</span> For the SDMI model on ImageNet100, the batch size was reduced to <span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">64</span> (instead of 256) due to the increased memory requirements from the two-encoder setup.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Toy models</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement the toy canonical SDMI and JMI prototypes in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Experimental setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, along with all benchmarks, each with a dedicated two-layer MLP encoder mapping <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2}\to\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2}\to\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. The encoder consists of a linear layer <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2\to 64)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2\to 64)</annotation></semantics></math> with bias, batch normalization, and ReLU activation, followed by a second linear layer <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(64\to 3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(64\to 3)</annotation></semantics></math> with batch normalization. The output is normalized to unit <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Method classification under SDMI/ JMI taxonomy</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present a comprehensive classification of representative SSRL methods under the SDMI/JMI framework as introduced in <a href="#S3" title="3 A Unified View of SSRL as MI Maximization ‣ Self-Supervised Representation Learning asMutual Information Maximization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Representative SSRL methods and their classification under the SDMI/ JMI taxonomy, with objective types.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EM/Joint</span></td>
<td id="A5.T7.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Objective Type</span></span>
<span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Explicit MI bound</span></span>
<span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vs</span></span>
<span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MI Surrogate</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A5.T7.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Paradigm</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
